# Framework # {#framework}

## Observer store ## {#framework-observer-store}

The user agent maintains an <dfn>observer store</dfn>. It is a [=set=] of weak references to {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} objects. The store is initially empty.

When an observer has been reclaimed by garbage collection, it must be [=set/removed=] from the store.

# The {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} interface # {#the-device-bound-sessions-observer-interface}

This interface can be used to observe [=device bound sessions=].

<pre class="idl">
[Exposed=Window, SecureContext]
interface DeviceBoundSessionsObserver {
  constructor(
    DeviceBoundSessionsObserverCallback callback,
    optional DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions options = {}
  );
  undefined observe();
  undefined disconnect();
  sequence&lt;DeviceBoundSessionsReport> takeRecords();
};

callback DeviceBoundSessionsObserverCallback = undefined (
  sequence&lt;DeviceBoundSessionsReport> reports,
  DeviceBoundSessionsObserver observer
);
</pre>

A {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} has an associated <dfn for="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver">callback</dfn> (a {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserverCallback}}) and an associated <dfn for="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver">options</dfn> (a {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions}}).

<div algorithm="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver constructor">
  When the <dfn constructor for="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver">DeviceBoundSessionsObserver(|callback|, |options|)</dfn> constructor is called:

  1. Set [=this=]'s [=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/callback=] to |callback|.
  1. Set [=this=]'s [=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/options=] to |options|.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn for="observer">inform</dfn> a {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} |observer| of a [=list=] of {{DeviceBoundSessionsReport}}s |reports|:

  1. [=Assert=]: |reports| is not [=list/is empty|empty=].
  1. [=Queue a global task=] on the [=networking task source=] given |observer|'s [=relevant global object=] to run these steps:
    1. If [=observer store=] does not [=list/contain=] |observer|, then return.
    1. [=Invoke=] |observer|'s [=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/callback=] with « |reports|, |observer| » and "`report`", and [=callback this value=] |observer|.

  Advisement: Callers of this algorithm must verify that |observer| is allowed to know about |reports| under the user agent's current policies, notably storage partitioning.
</div>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions}} dictionary ## {#options-dictionary}

<pre class="idl">
dictionary DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions {
  AbortSignal signal;
};
</pre>

<dl dfn-for="DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions">
  : <dfn dict-member>signal</dfn>
  :: The {{AbortSignal/abort}} event stops the observer from receiving further reports.
</dl>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/observe()}} method ## {#observe-method}

<div algorithm="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver.observe()">
  When <dfn method for=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver>observe()</dfn> is called:

  1. Let |signal| be [=this=]'s [=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/options=][{{DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions/signal}}].
  1. If |signal| [=map/exists=] and is [=AbortSignal/aborted=], then return.
  1. If [=observer store=] [=list/contains=] [=this=], then return.
  1. [=set/Append=] a weak reference to [=this=] to [=observer store=].
  1. If |signal| [=map/exists=], then [=AbortSignal/add|add the following abort steps=] to |signal|:
    1. Call [=this=]'s {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/disconnect()}}.
  1. Let |reports| be the result of [=observer/collecting past reports=] for [=this=].
  1. If |reports| is not [=list/is empty|empty=], then [=observer/inform=] [=this=] of |reports|.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn for="observer">collect past reports</dfn> for a {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} |observer|:

  1. Let |environment| be |observer|'s [=relevant settings object=].
  1. Let |reports| be a new [=list=].
  1. [=list/For each=] |sessions by id| of [=session store=]'s [=map/values=]:
    1. [=list/For each=] |session| of |sessions by id|'s [=map/values=]:
      1. If [=determine session visibility=] given |environment| and |session| does not return "visible", then [=iteration/continue=].
      1. Let |session report| be the result of [=creating an established session report=] given |session|.
      1. [=list/Append=] |session report| to |reports|.
  1. Return |reports|.
</div>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/disconnect()}} method ## {#disconnect-method}

<div algorithm="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver.disconnect()">
  When <dfn method for=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver>disconnect()</dfn> is called:

  1. [=set/Remove=] [=this=] from [=observer store=].

  User agents may want to also clean up previously set up {{AbortSignal/abort}} steps and remove garbage-collected references from the store.
</div>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/takeRecords()}} method ## {#take-records-method}

<div algorithm="DeviceBoundSessionsObserver.takeRecords()">
  When <dfn method for=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver>takeRecords()</dfn> is called:

  1. Let |reports| be the result of [=observer/collecting past reports=] for [=this=].
  1. Return |reports|.
</div>

## Report types ## {#report-types}

<pre class="idl">
enum DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind {
  "session"
};

dictionary DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport {
  required DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind type;
  required DOMString sessionOrigin;
  required DOMString sessionId;
  required DOMString refreshUrl;
  required DOMHighResTimeStamp creationTime;
};

typedef DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport DeviceBoundSessionsReport;
</pre>

### Established session report ### {#established-session-report}

A <dfn dictionary>DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport</dfn> represents a [=device bound session=].

<dl dfn-for="DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport">
  : <dfn dict-member>type</dfn>
  :: Must be {{DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind/"session"}}.
  : <dfn dict-member>sessionOrigin</dfn>
  :: The [=serialization of an origin|serialized=] [=session scope/origin=] of the [=device bound session=]'s [=device bound session/session scope=].
  : <dfn dict-member>sessionId</dfn>
  :: The [=device bound session=]'s [=device bound session/session identifier=].
  : <dfn dict-member>refreshUrl</dfn>
  :: The [=URL serializer|serialized=] [=device bound session/refresh URL=] of the [=device bound session=].
  : <dfn dict-member>creationTime</dfn>
  :: The [=duration from=] the [=Unix epoch=] to the [=device bound session=]'s [=device bound session/creation time=].
</dl>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>create an established session report</dfn> given a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |report| be a new {{DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport}} dictionary with:
      : {{DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport/type}}
      :: {{DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind/"session"}}.
      : {{DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport/sessionOrigin}}
      :: The [=serialization of an origin=] given |session|'s [=device bound session/session scope=]'s [=session scope/origin=].
      : {{DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport/sessionId}}
      :: |session|'s [=device bound session/session identifier=].
      : {{DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport/refreshUrl}}
      :: The [=URL serializer=] of |session|'s [=device bound session/refresh URL=].
      : {{DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport/creationTime}}
      :: The [=duration from=] the [=Unix epoch=] to |session|'s [=device bound session/creation time=].
  1. Return |report|.
</div>

# Session reports visibility # {#session-reports-visibility}

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn export>determine session visibility</dfn> given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
  1. If |url| is not |session|'s [=device bound session/refresh URL=]:
    1. If the result of running [=algorithms/determine if a URL is in scope=] with |url| and |session| is false, then return "hidden".
  1. If |environment| [=environment/has storage access=], then return "visible".
  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

<!-- This is an alternative to checking for [=environment/has storage access=] above.

<div algorithm>
To <dfn>check whether credentials would be included</dfn>, given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
    Note: |url| can be reused from an earlier step if merged into the visibility algo.
  1. Let |request| be a new [=request=] whose [=request/URL=] is |url|, [=request/method=] is \``GET`\`, [=request/client=] is |environment|, [=request/mode=] is "`same-origin`", and [=request/credentials mode=] is "`include`".
  1. [=list/For each=] |credential| of |session|'s [=device bound session/session credentials=]:
    1. If |credential|'s [=session credential/type=] is "`cookie`", and a cookie with |credential|'s [=session credential/attributes=] would be attached to |request| (see [[RFC6265#cookie]]), then return "visible".
  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

-->

<div class="example" id="session-visibility-example">

  Issue: Consider making this a WPT instead.

  Given the following (incomplete) session definition:

  ```json
  {
    "session_identifier": "session_id",
    "refresh_url": "/refresh",
    "scope": {
      "origin": "https://example.com",
      "include_site": true,
      "scope_specification" : [
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "sites.example.com", "path": "/" },
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "*.example.com", "path": "/static" }
      ]
    },
    "credentials": [{
      "type": "cookie",
      "name": "auth_cookie",
      "attributes": "Domain=example.com; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict"
    }]
  }
  ```

  The following table illustrates whether `session_id` is visible to various execution environments:

  <table>
    <tr>
        <th>Creation URL</th>
        <th>Storage access</th>
        <th>Visible?</th>
        <th>Reason</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/account`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>In scope of `session_id`, has storage access.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sub.example.com/app`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Also in scope of `session_id`, by its `include_site`.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Refresh URL bypasses scope check.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Embedded without storage access</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>No access to 1P `example.com` storage.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sites.example.com/a`</td>
        <td>N/A</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>URL matches the `sites.example.com/` exclusion rule.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://app.example.com/static/index.html`</td>
        <td>N/A</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>URL matches the `*.example.com/static` exclusion rule.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</div>

# Changes to other specifications # {#changes-to-other-specifications}

## Changes to the DBSC specification ## {#changes-to-dbsc}

Issue: Avoid deep monkey-patching here: open a PR against [[dbsc-1]], then remove this section.

In [=device bound session=], add the following item:

: <dfn for="device bound session">creation time</dfn>
:: The [=current coarsened wall time=] at which this session was created.

In [=create a session=]:

1. After setting the [=device bound session/expiration timestamp=], also set [=device bound session/creation time=].
